# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD triple-1 63869 black
ADD doublesplit-1 41678 black
ADD axle-1 3705 black
CONNECT axle-1.axle1 -> triple-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-1.axle2 -> doublesplit-1.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Starts the input block by joining a triple connector and a double-split connector nose to nose on one long axle.
STEP 2
ADD sixfivethreesix-1 6536 black
CONNECT sixfivethreesix-1.axlehole1 -> axle-1.axle3 LOCKED
WHY Caps the free end of the same axle with another perpendicular connector, finishing the input block's three-connector stack.
STEP 3
ADD pin-1 43093 blue
ADD gear-1 3647 darkbluishgray
CONNECT gear-1.axlehole1 -> pin-1.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Builds a small fixed-gear sub-assembly on its own, separate from the input block, ready to plug in later.
STEP 4
ADD apin-1 18651 black
ADD apin-2 18651 black
ADD bush-1 3713 red
ADD bush-2 3713 red
CONNECT bush-1.axlehole1 -> apin-1.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-2.axlehole1 -> apin-2.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Builds two identical pin-and-bush units, the outer tip of each capped with a bush so it can't slide out later.
STEP 5
ADD drivering-1 26287 red
CONNECT drivering-1.axlehole1 -> apin-1.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT drivering-1.axlehole1 -> apin-2.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Joins the two pin units end to end through the long driving ring, making one output rod with a bush at each end.
STEP 6
CONNECT pin-1.pin1 -> doublesplit-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT apin-1.pin1 -> sixfivethreesix-1.hole1 STIFF
WHY Plugs the small fixed-gear unit and the long output rod into the input block's two free round holes, tying all three sub-builds together.
STEP 7
ADD diff-1 6573 darkbluishgray
ADD bevel-1 6589 tan
ADD bevel-2 6589 tan
ADD axle-2 4519 black
CONNECT bevel-1.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT bevel-2.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-2.axle3 -> diff-1.hole1~ TURNS
WHY Locks two bevel gears onto a short axle and drops them inside the first differential housing, with the axle riding free in the housing's near hole.
STEP 8
ADD conn18654-1 18654 darkbluishgray
ADD bevel-3 6589 tan
ADD gear10928-1 10928 darkbluishgray
ADD axle-3 3705 black
CONNECT bevel-3.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-3.axle2 -> diff-1.hole2~ TURNS
CONNECT conn18654-1.hole1 -> axle-3.axle3 TURNS
CONNECT gear10928-1.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle4 LOCKED
WHY Builds the first differential's output shaft: a third bevel gear through the housing's far hole, a round spacer, and a reinforced gear locked on the tip.
STEP 9
ADD diff-2 6573 darkbluishgray
ADD bevel-4 6589 tan
ADD bevel-5 6589 tan
ADD axle-4 4519 black
CONNECT bevel-4.axlehole1 -> axle-4.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT bevel-5.axlehole1 -> axle-4.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-4.axle3 -> diff-2.hole1~ TURNS
WHY Repeats step 7 for the second differential housing, so the gearbox ends up with two matching gear units side by side.
STEP 10
ADD conn18654-2 18654 darkbluishgray
ADD bevel-6 6589 tan
ADD gear10928-2 10928 darkbluishgray
ADD axle-5 3705 black
CONNECT bevel-6.axlehole1 -> axle-5.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-5.axle2 -> diff-2.hole2~ TURNS
CONNECT conn18654-2.hole1 -> axle-5.axle3 TURNS
CONNECT gear10928-2.axlehole1 -> axle-5.axle4 LOCKED
WHY Repeats step 8 for the second housing, giving it its own spaced, reinforced output gear.
STEP 11
CONNECT axle-2.axle3 -> triple-1.hole2~ TURNS
CONNECT axle-4.axle3 -> triple-1.hole3~ TURNS
MESH gear-1.teeth gear10928-1.teeth
WHY Swings both differential units back onto the input block's spare holes and brings the fixed gear into mesh with the first output gear.
STEP 12
ADD triple-2 63869 black
ADD doublesplit-2 41678 black
ADD axle-6 3705 black
CONNECT axle-6.axle1 -> triple-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-6.axle2 -> doublesplit-2.axlehole1~ LOCKED
WHY Builds a second input-style block, a mirror of step 1, for the far end of the gearbox.
STEP 13
ADD sixfivethreesix-2 6536 black
ADD pin2780-1 2780 black
CONNECT sixfivethreesix-2.axlehole1 -> axle-6.axle3 LOCKED
CONNECT pin2780-1.pin1 -> triple-2.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Caps the second block's axle the same way as step 2, then plugs a friction pin into its triple connector for a later attachment point.
STEP 14
ADD apin-4 18651 black
ADD apin-5 18651 black
ADD bush-5 3713 red
ADD bush-6 3713 red
CONNECT bush-5.axlehole1 -> apin-4.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-6.axlehole1 -> apin-5.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Repeats step 4 to build the second output rod's two pin-and-bush units.
STEP 15
ADD drivering-2 26287 red
CONNECT drivering-2.axlehole1 -> apin-4.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT drivering-2.axlehole1 -> apin-5.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Joins the second pair of pin units through the second driving ring, completing the second output rod.
STEP 16
ADD pin3749-1 3749 tan
ADD gear-2 3647 darkbluishgray
CONNECT gear-2.axlehole1 -> pin3749-1.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Builds a second small fixed-gear unit the same way as step 3, using the frictionless tan pin left in the inventory.
STEP 17
CONNECT pin3749-1.pin1 -> doublesplit-2.hole1~ TURNS
CONNECT apin-4.pin1 -> sixfivethreesix-2.hole1 STIFF
WHY Plugs the second fixed-gear unit and the second output rod into the second block, mirroring step 6.
STEP 18
CONNECT apin-5.pin1 -> triple-2.hole2~ STIFF
MESH gear-2.teeth gear10928-2.teeth
WHY Closes the far end of the gearbox: the second rod's last free pin grips the second block's triple connector while the second fixed gear meshes with the second output gear.
STEP 19
ADD motor-1 99499c01 lightbluishgray
CONNECT axle-1.axle4 -> motor-1.shaft? LOCKED
WHY Locks the motor's output shaft onto the input block's last free axle end, ready to drive the whole gear train.
